## API conventions (`/api/*`)
- English JSON field names; Spanish only in UI layer
- Key routes: `/health`, `/conditions`, `/settings`, `/images`, `/images/content`, `/screen`, `/screen/path`
- Image browse restricted under `data/` (see `api/images.py`)
- Models preloaded in `api/registry.py` at startup

---

## Frontend conventions
- **Brand:** ByteAI in `es.productName` and header
- **Styling:** Prefer `pro-*` classes and CSS variables in `index.css` — avoid custom Tailwind color tokens in `@apply` (breaks PostCSS)
- **State:** Screening logic in `hooks/useScreening.ts`; auth/theme in `context/`
- **Mobile:** `MobileNav` + tab panels on small screens; desktop uses multi-column grid
- **Auth (UI):** Dev gate via `AuthContext` — user `root` / password `admin` (localStorage; not real backend auth yet)
- **Timeline:** `useStudyTimeline` (localStorage `byteai-timeline-v2`, max 20; migrates from `byteai-timeline` when possible) stores full `ScreeningResponse` + folder context; click restores informe; re-export PDF from entry
- **Viewer:** `ImagingViewport` — zoom (wheel/buttons), pan when zoomed, invert, reset; prev/next study buttons
- **Navigation:** Folder mode — `↑`/`↓` or `j`/`k` to change study; optional auto-advance after screening
- **Batch:** `useBatchScreening` + `BatchScreeningPanel` — sequential `POST /api/screen/path` over folder list, progress, cancel, summary table, row opens study
- **PDF export:** `ExportReportButton` → `generateScreeningPdf()` — thumbnail (via `imageToPdfDataUrl`), findings table + detail cards, footer with screened conditions list, `doc.save()`. Pass `imageUrl` and `screenedAt` from screening state. No `window.print()`.
- **Viewer W/L:** CSS presets in `viewportWindowLevel.ts` (not DICOM). **Clinical review:** checkbox in `ResultsDashboard` persists per study label in `localStorage` (`byteai-reviewed-*`).
- **Visual semantics:** Amber / `pro-priority-flagged` = derivar revisión; emerald / `pro-priority-clear` = rutina; teal accent on interactive elements and active workflow step only
- **Paused tracks:** Do not add ML training or production auth/Docker/CI unless user unpause B/C

When adding UI copy, only edit `frontend/src/i18n/es.ts`.

